<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ki Ageng Pemanahan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1584</span> · Also known as Ki Gede Pemanahan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ki Ageng Pemanahan was a Javanese noble who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadiwijaya">Hadiwijaya</a> of Pajang and helped him defeat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arya-penangsang">Arya Penangsang</a> in the succession war after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trenggana">Trenggana</a>'s death. As a reward he received the land of Mataram, where he founded a settlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kotagede">Kotagede</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panembahan-senapati">Sutawijaya</a>, known as Panembahan Senapati, threw off Pajang's authority and founded the Mataram Sultanate.</p></div>
